## Spring Boot Redis Cache Setup

```xml
<!-- pom.xml -->
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-data-redis</artifactId>
</dependency>
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-cache</artifactId>
</dependency>
```

```yaml
# application.yml
spring:
  redis:
    host: localhost
    port: 6379
    password: ${REDIS_PASSWORD}
    lettuce:
      pool:
        max-active: 8
        max-idle: 8
        min-idle: 0
  cache:
    type: redis
    redis:
      time-to-live: 600000  # 10 minutes default TTL
      cache-null-values: false  # Don't cache null (optional)
```

```java
@Configuration
@EnableCaching
public class CacheConfig {

    @Bean
    public RedisCacheManager cacheManager(RedisConnectionFactory connectionFactory) {
        // Per-cache TTL configuration:
        Map<String, RedisCacheConfiguration> cacheConfigs = new HashMap<>();

        // Product catalog: changes rarely → long TTL
        cacheConfigs.put("products", RedisCacheConfiguration.defaultCacheConfig()
            .entryTtl(Duration.ofHours(24))
            .serializeValuesWith(serializationPair()));  // Use JSON

        // User sessions: medium TTL
        cacheConfigs.put("userSessions", RedisCacheConfiguration.defaultCacheConfig()
            .entryTtl(Duration.ofMinutes(30))
            .serializeValuesWith(serializationPair()));

        // Exchange rates: change frequently → short TTL
        cacheConfigs.put("exchangeRates", RedisCacheConfiguration.defaultCacheConfig()
            .entryTtl(Duration.ofMinutes(5))
            .serializeValuesWith(serializationPair()));

        return RedisCacheManager.builder(connectionFactory)
            .cacheDefaults(RedisCacheConfiguration.defaultCacheConfig()
                .entryTtl(Duration.ofMinutes(10))  // Default
                .serializeValuesWith(serializationPair()))
            .withInitialCacheConfigurations(cacheConfigs)
            .build();
    }

    private RedisSerializationContext.SerializationPair<Object> serializationPair() {
        return RedisSerializationContext.SerializationPair
            .fromSerializer(new GenericJackson2JsonRedisSerializer());
    }
}
```

## @Cacheable, @CacheEvict, @CachePut

```java
@Service
public class ProductService {

    // @Cacheable: cache result; return cache on subsequent calls
    @Cacheable(value = "products", key = "#productId")
    public Product findById(Long productId) {
        log.info("Cache MISS — loading from DB for product {}", productId);
        return productRepository.findById(productId)
            .orElseThrow(() -> new NotFoundException("Product " + productId));
        // First call: hits DB, stores in Redis as: products::42 → {Product JSON}
        // Subsequent calls: returns from Redis, DB never called
    }

    // Conditional caching — don't cache non-existent:
    @Cacheable(value = "products", key = "#productId", unless = "#result == null")
    public Product findByIdOrNull(Long productId) {
        return productRepository.findById(productId).orElse(null);
    }

    // @CacheEvict: remove from cache when data changes
    @CacheEvict(value = "products", key = "#product.id")
    @Transactional
    public Product update(Product product) {
        return productRepository.save(product);
        // After save, Redis entry products::42 is deleted
        // Next findById(42) will reload from DB
    }

    // @CachePut: always calls method AND updates cache
    @CachePut(value = "products", key = "#product.id")
    @Transactional
    public Product updateAndCache(Product product) {
        return productRepository.save(product);
        // Different from @CacheEvict: updates cache with new value immediately
        // No stale window — cache has the latest value right away
    }

    // Evict entire cache region:
    @CacheEvict(value = "products", allEntries = true)
    @Scheduled(cron = "0 0 * * * *")  // Hourly
    public void clearProductCache() {
        log.info("Clearing entire product cache");
    }
}
```

## Cache-Aside Pattern (Manual Control)

```java
@Service
public class InventoryService {

    private final RedisTemplate<String, InventoryStatus> redisTemplate;
    private final InventoryRepository inventoryRepository;

    public InventoryStatus getStatus(String productId) {
        String key = "inventory:" + productId;

        // 1. Check cache:
        InventoryStatus cached = redisTemplate.opsForValue().get(key);
        if (cached != null) {
            return cached;  // Cache HIT
        }

        // 2. Cache MISS — load from DB:
        InventoryStatus status = inventoryRepository.findByProductId(productId);

        // 3. Store in cache with TTL:
        redisTemplate.opsForValue().set(key, status, Duration.ofMinutes(5));

        return status;
    }

    public void updateInventory(String productId, int quantity) {
        inventoryRepository.updateQuantity(productId, quantity);

        // Invalidate cache:
        redisTemplate.delete("inventory:" + productId);
        // Next getStatus() will reload from DB
    }
}
```

## Distributed Lock with Redisson

```java
// Preventing duplicate processing:
@Service
public class PaymentService {

    private final RedissonClient redisson;

    public PaymentResult processPayment(String orderId, PaymentRequest request) {
        // Distributed lock: only one instance processes this order at a time
        RLock lock = redisson.getLock("payment-lock:" + orderId);

        try {
            // Try to acquire lock, wait max 5s, hold max 30s:
            boolean acquired = lock.tryLock(5, 30, TimeUnit.SECONDS);
            if (!acquired) {
                throw new PaymentInProgressException("Payment already being processed");
            }

            // Check idempotency first:
            if (paymentRepository.existsByOrderId(orderId)) {
                return paymentRepository.findByOrderId(orderId);
            }

            return chargeAndSave(request);
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
            throw new PaymentException("Interrupted while acquiring lock");
        } finally {
            if (lock.isHeldByCurrentThread()) {
                lock.unlock();
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## Production Reality

Always serialize to JSON (not Java serialization) — JSON survives code refactoring and can be read externally for debugging. Monitor cache hit rate via Redis INFO stats or Spring Boot Actuator (`cache.gets` metric tagged with `result=hit/miss`). A hit rate below 80% suggests the TTL is too short or you're caching the wrong things. Watch Redis memory usage — set `maxmemory` and an eviction policy (`allkeys-lru` is safe for caches) so Redis doesn't run out of memory.
